{"slug": "blue-cheese-coleslaw", "nyt_id": 788210058, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/788210058-blue-cheese-coleslaw", "name": "Blue Cheese Coleslaw", "author": "Ali Slagle", "description": "The savory funkiness of blue cheese races through the creamy dressing of this simply spectacular slaw. In a nod to the crudités that are often served with blue cheese dip, thinly sliced celery and carrots are added; you could also toss in thinly sliced scallions, red onion, parsley, chives – even green apple. Eat alongside something rich, like Buffalo wings, hot dogs, fried chicken or meatloaf.", "servings": {"text": "4-6 servings", "min": 4, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 15, "cook_minutes": 5, "total_minutes": 20, "raw": {"total": "20 min", "prep": "PT0H15M", "cook": "PT0H5M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "3 ounces crumbled blue cheese (about ½ cup), plus more for serving", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "crumbled blue cheese (about ½ cup)", "preparation": "plus more for serving", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "½ cup buttermilk", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "buttermilk", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "¼ cup sour cream or whole-milk Greek yogurt", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "sour cream or whole-milk greek yogurt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "¼ cup mayonnaise", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "mayonnaise", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "Juice from 1 lemon (3 tablespoons)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "juice from 1 lemon (3 tablespoons)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 large garlic clove, finely chopped or grated", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "large garlic clove", "preparation": "finely chopped or grated", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "Salt and black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "2 pounds thinly sliced green or red cabbage (about 10 cups or ½ large head – or use store bought slaw blend)", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "lb", "item": "thinly sliced green or red cabbage (about 10 cups or ½ large head – or use store bought slaw blend)", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "4 celery stalks, thinly sliced, plus any leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "celery stalks", "preparation": "thinly sliced, plus any leaves", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "2 carrots, grated on the large holes of a box grater", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "carrots", "preparation": "grated on the large holes of a box grater", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "In a microwave-safe medium bowl or large liquid measuring cup, microwave the blue cheese until just warm, about 20 seconds. Stir with a spoon to smooth, then add the buttermilk, sour cream, mayonnaise, lemon juice, garlic and a few grinds of pepper. Stir to combine. Season to taste with salt and pepper."}, {"position": 2, "text": "In a large bowl, toss the cabbage, celery and carrots with a pinch of salt. Add most of the dressing and toss to coat, adding more dressing as needed to thinly coat. Top with more black pepper and blue cheese as you like. Serve right away, leave out for up to 2 hours, or cover and refrigerate for up to 3 days."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 197.5, "protein_g": 6.1, "carbohydrates_g": 17.0, "fat_g": 13.1, "saturated_fat_g": 4.4, "trans_fat_g": 0.1, "cholesterol_m